  <div class="section-label">Phase 3 — Weber County Segment</div>
  <h2>1800 North to 4000 South (West Haven)</h2>

  <p>The Phase 3 segment runs north from 1800 North in West Point to 4000 South in West Haven — the portion under State Environmental Study.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %} UDOT's Draft State Environmental Study, published November 6, 2026, identifies a Preferred Alternative along 5100 West and maps its proposed right-of-way parcel by parcel in the Right-of-Way Impacts mapbook in Volume 2.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %}{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol2-nov2026" %} The mapbook is a draft: UDOT says impacts "may be refined during the final design and right-of-way acquisition phases."{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %}</p>

  <p>UDOT's earlier stated standard footprint was <strong>250 feet</strong>, designed to accommodate four travel lanes separated by a median and flanked by multi-use trail corridors.{% cite "udot-ses-build" %} The draft study's maps, not this rule of thumb, now show where the proposed right-of-way falls, including around interchanges and frontage roads. Under UDOT's definitions, a property is a relocation when an existing structure is in or within 15 feet of the proposed right-of-way, and a partial acquisition when only land is needed.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %}</p>

