  <p>Other draft land impacts: about 106 acres converted from other zoning to transportation use, about 2.4 acres of one Agricultural Protection Area near 4000 South and 5100 West, and land near 33 water-right points of diversion, where UDOT says it would relocate wells or diversions or compensate owners for the water right.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %} UDOT says impacted property owners and businesses would receive "fair and just compensation" under the Utah Relocation Assistance Act.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol1-nov2026" %}{% cite "udot-acquisition-guide" %}</p>

  <div class="section-label">Phase 4 — Long-Range Segment</div>
  <h2>4000 South to Box Elder County Line</h2>

  <p>The segment north of 4000 South toward the Box Elder County line is long-range. In the Wasatch Front Regional Council 2023–2050 plan, 4000 South to 900 South is in Phase 3 (2043–2050) and 900 South to I-15 is unfunded.{% cite "wfrc-rtp-roadway-lines-2023" %} No State Environmental Study has been started for this segment, and no alignment, footprint, or design has been approved. UDOT has, however, programmed a corridor study to re-evaluate the 2009 North Legacy study from 4000 South north to Box Elder County; see the <a href="phase-4-longrange.html">Phase 4 page</a>.{% cite "wfrc-transcom-nov2025-udot-sr177-study" %}{% cite "udot-draft-stip-2027-2032" %}</p>

